            <ArticleTitle>Psychological factors leading to amputations in adults.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>196-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Psychological factors may lead to a small number of amputations in adults. They may be classified as being due to: 1. chronic pain syndrome; 2. artefactualists; 3. self-mutilation; 4. attempted murder. An understanding of these potential factors will make the amputee clinic team aware of this problem, and help them deal with the rehabilitation of the patient.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
